Somewhere along the line, you got your god angry at you (even though
you are piously aligned.  I don't know what you did (sacrifice a human?
kill your pet?  Just pray so often to annoy him?  Convert an altar
to another god?)

In any case, sacrificing is the most direct way of trying to get
back into His good graces.  Whenever 'you have a feeling of inadequacy'
it means that your choice of sacrifice was not terribly convincing.
Newt and kobold corpses just won't cut it.  You need to sacrifice
some 'real' monsters.  For awhile, your god will seem "slightly
mollified"; he forgives you when he is "mollified".  That takes
care of his anger at least.  Your pray timeout would be a different
story.

